%U A401049 1,4,3,2,1,4,3,2,1,4,3,2
%N A401049 Period 4: repeat [1, 4, 3, 2].
%C A401049 Cylinder firing order for early Volkswagen and Porsche flat-four engines. The designer chose a diagonal sequence across the crankcase (1-Right, 4-Left, 3-Left, 2-Right). This geometry balances primary and secondary forces across opposing horizontally opposed pistons and equalizes cooling air distribution.
%D A401049 J. B. Heywood, Internal Combustion Engine Fundamentals, McGraw-Hill, 1988.
%D A401049 C. F. Taylor, The Internal Combustion Engine in Theory and Practice, Vol. 2, MIT Press, 1985.
%H A401049 American National Standards Institute (ANSI), <a href="https://webstore.ansi.org/standards/sae/sae8242022">SAE J824: Engine Rotation and Cylinder Numbering</a>
%H A401049 Automotive Engine Mechanics, <a href="https://automotiveenginemechanics.tpub.com/TM-5-2815-232-14/TM-5-2815-232-140026.htm">Engine Design: Cylinder Location and Firing Order</a>
%H A401049 SAE International, <a href="https://www.sae.org/standards/j824_202206-engine-rotation-cylinder-numbering">Standard J824: Engine Rotation and Cylinder Numbering</a>
%H A401049 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (0,0,0,1).
%F A401049 a(n) = a(n-4).
%F A401049 G.f.: (1 + 4*x + 3*x^2 + 2*x^3)/((1 - x)*(1 + x)*(1 + x^2)).
%F A401049 E.g.f.: 2*cosh(x) - cos(x) + 3*sinh(x) + sin(x). - _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 15 2026
%Y A401049 Cf. A070352, A385491, A385634.
